WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.700
Hey, welcome to Models and Agents, episode 90 for June 23, 2026. Lots of news to walk through.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:12.200
Let's start with what actually matters. Open AI just shipped a full cyber defense stack,

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:19.400
GPT 5.5 cyber plus codec security and patch the planet. So defenders can now scan, validate,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:26.980
and patch a machine speed inside existing workflows. The daybreak expansion adds a dedicated GPT 5.5

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:33.980
cyber model that traces vulnerabilities, validates issues, and generates patches. A codec security

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:40.660
plugin runs deep scans and exports results to tools teams already use. A new cyber partner program

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:47.600
pairs open AI with trail of bits and hacker 1 for direct maintainer support. The entire stack

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.300
limits itself to authorize defensive work and requires human review before any remediation.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.140
Teams can now move from initial findings to merged fixes without leaving their current code

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.520
environment. Security vendors are expected to announce integrations through the partner program

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:09.940
in the coming weeks. This development lands in the ongoing safety and policy conversation

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:16.460
the show has tracked since episode 89. It tests whether frontier models can deliver reliable audit

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.180
trails in high stakes defensive settings without expanding offensive capabilities.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:28.900
Alibaba released Happy Horse 1.1, a 15 billion parameter unified self-attention transformer.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.720
The model processes text, image, video, and audio in a single forward pass.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.020
It adds multi-image reference to video support for consistent character identity across shots,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:48.140
improved motion modeling, and zero drift lip sync for up to 15 seconds of 1080p output.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:55.940
Happy Horse 1.1 sits at number two on the artificial analysis video arena leaderboards ahead of Google

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:03.740
VO 3.1 in both text-to-video and image-to-video tasks. The upgrade is available now through the alibaba

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:11.340
cloud model studio API with a 40% discount for the first two weeks. Builders working on advertising

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:17.360
or serialized video should test the reference to video workflow to check whether identity

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:24.380
consistency reduces post-production work. Sakana launched Fugu, a multi-agent orchestration system that

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:29.740
roots queries across a pool of swappable models through a single open AI compatible API.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:37.640
Fugu Ultra uses fixed pricing of $5 per million input tokens and $30 per million output tokens.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:46.620
On live code bench, the system scores 92.9 to 93.2 above cloud-fable 5 at 89.8.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:55.120
On GPQA diamond, it reaches 95.5. The service remains closed source and is currently restricted

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:03.740
from the EU and EEA, while GDPR alignment continues. This sits inside the frontier models arc covered on

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:09.700
episode 89. It shows whether orchestration layers can match single model frontier performance without

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:17.180
direct access to the highest capability endpoints. Nvidia released a set of trusted 24.7 AI privacy

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:23.380
scanner for purpose built for telecom network operations. The agents run continuous monitoring,

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.820
anomaly detection, and automated remediation inside existing network infrastructure.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.300
No public install commands or pricing details were shared in the announcement.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.800
The focus is on reliability and auditability for always on carrier environments.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.560
Network teams should watch for the first customer deployments to see how the agents

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.660
handle live traffic without human intervention. Microsoft published the first two posts in its

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.720
agent framework series showing how to build a CLI style claw agent with planning, tools,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.240
memory, and safe execution. The harness wraps a language model in a controllable loop and is

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:07.800
demonstrated on a personal finance assistant example. No license or pricing is stated.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:13.360
The post position the framework as an open building block, developers wanting a lightweight

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.340
alternative to heavier orchestration libraries should clone the examples and run the finance assistant

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:26.240
demo locally this week. Researchers released self harness, a three-stage loop that lets an agent

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:32.980
mine its own failure traces, propose minimal harness edits, and validate them through regression testing.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:43.220
On terminal dash bench dash 2.0 the system delivered 33 to 60% relative gains across minimax m2.5,

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:51.900
QN3.5 to 35ba3b and GLM5 without changing the underlying model or tools.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:58.420
The method requires deterministic verifiers and is best suited to measurable environments such as

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:05.320
DevOps pipelines. Teams maintaining custom agents should review the paper to see whether adding a

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:11.320
weakness mining step to their evaluation harness reduces manual prompt tuning. Simon Willison

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:20.200
ported the 0.2 billion Moebius image in-painting model to ONNX and web GPU so it runs entirely in

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:27.900
the browser after a roughly 1.3 gigabyte download. The demo at SimonW.github.io slash

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:35.380
Moebius hyphen web lets users open any image, mark regions, and run in-painting with caching via

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:41.540
the cache storage API. The project was built with cloud code and publishes converted weights to

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:47.400
hugging face. Anyone experimenting with client-side vision tools should open the demo in Chrome or

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:54.220
Firefox and test in-painting on their own photos to judge whether the 1.3 gigabyte first load cost

00:05:54.220 --> 00:06:01.880
is acceptable for their use case. Niels Raga updated papers with code.co with SOTA badges and

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:08.040
new trending score combining GitHub stars and hugging face artifact velocity and support for

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:16.620
external third-party evaluations. New benchmarks include ImageNet 10%, 3-dimensional semantic segmentation,

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:24.460
and object counting. The site now also lives at paperswithco.de. Researchers tracking SOTA should

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:30.660
visit the video classification or reasoning task pages to see how the new external Eval support

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:37.620
surfaces numbers beyond the original papers. Okay, let's pop the hood on the Moebius browser demo.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:46.320
Running a model entirely client-side starts with exporting a pie-torch graph to ONNX using opset 18

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:53.400
so every operator becomes part of a portable computation graph. The export records dynamic axes

00:06:53.400 --> 00:07:00.020
so batch and spatial dimensions stay flexible, but it also drops any pie-torch specific control flow

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:08.200
that cannot be expressed in the ONNX operator set. Once converted, the 1.24 gigabyte weight file

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:14.480
must be fetched and cached through the cache storage API, which keeps the tensors resident across

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:22.580
reloads and reduces later loads from minutes to seconds. Operators without direct web GPU equivalents

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:30.380
are emulated, adding measurable latency on every forward pass. When the model stays under roughly 1.5

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:36.100
gigabytes and the workload is embarrassingly parallel, such as single image in-painting,

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:42.820
the approach wins on privacy and zero install deployment. The moment you need custom CUDA kernels

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:49.120
or multi-gigabyte context, the same model still belongs on a server with a proper GPU runtime.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.880
So when should you actually reach for the browser version versus the alternative? Choose the

00:07:54.880 --> 00:08:00.360
browser path when the workload fits the size and parallelism constraints and you need immediate

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:07.860
privacy or offline access. Open the Moebius in-painting demo and test region removal on your own photos

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:13.340
to judge whether the 1.3 gigabyte download fits your client-side vision workflow.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:20.500
Root a multi-step coding task through Sikana Fugu Ultra and compare token cost and output quality

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:27.280
against a direct clawed or GPT 5.5 call. Run the Microsoft agent framework, finance,

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:33.000
hyphen, assistant, example locally to see how the claw harness structures tool use and memory without

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:39.600
heavier frameworks. Check the updated peepers with code.co task pages for video classification

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:46.240
or reasoning to see external benchmark numbers that were previously hidden. OpenAI's cyber partner

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:51.000
program is expected to announce initial security vendor integrations in the coming weeks.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.180
Alibaba plans to roll out agent run and star ops agent platforms on its new European data centers

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:04.840
later this year. Sikana will continue expanding the Fugu model pool and is working on GDPR

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:11.140
compliant routing for EU and EEA availability. Tomorrow keep an eye on the first announced

